  "revision": "2026-09-11",
  "$comment": [
    "THE appearance vocabulary. One declaration, four consumers:",
    "  loom         src/lib/utils/assist-widget.ts  (WIDGET_APPEARANCE_KEYS, toWidgetAppearance, buildWidgetEmbedCode)",
    "  clairvoyance app/schemas/breeze_buddy/widget_config.py  (WidgetAppearance)",
    "  nautilus     shopify-apps/{buddy-assist,breeze-buddy}/extensions/buddy-assist-widget/assets/buddy-assist-loader.js",
    "  the widget   packages/breeze-buddy-assist-widget/src/BuddyAssist.svelte  (the custom-element attributes)",
    "",
    "Those four used to be four hand-maintained lists of the same words, and they drifted:",
    "theme, surface_color, text_color and user_bubble_color were missing from three of them",
    "until 2026-09-11, which meant dark mode could not reach a Shopify storefront at all.",
    "",
    "consoleField \u2014 the WidgetConfig field the console form binds, or null.",
    "consoleOwned \u2014 whether a console save REPLACES this key. A key that is not owned is carried",
    "  through untouched by mergeWidgetAppearance, so a value only a storefront or a hosted",
    "  theme.css ever set is not deleted by someone opening the Appearance tab.",
    "emptyIsUnset \u2014 \"\" means \"use the widget default\", so the key is omitted rather than stored.",
    "",
    "This file is copied VERBATIM into the other two repos (they are separate git repos, so there",
    "is no import that can span them). `node scripts/sync-widget-vocabulary.mjs` does the copying.",
    "Each repo has a test that checks its own structures against its copy AND pins `revision`, so a",
    "half-finished sync fails three builds instead of shipping a silent drift. BUMP `revision`",
    "whenever `entries` changes, and update the pinned constant in all three tests \u2014 that is the",
    "deliberate act the pin exists to force."
  ],
